      "rationale": "This canonical entry carries the simplification attribute and includes deleteFreshFrame, the extensional Map fact that deleting fresh key 1 restores SC. Stage 1 compiles it into VERIFICATION before every kprove command and never proves its exact statement in a rule-free module, so the trusted fact controls the entry's classification even though the same inventory entry also contains the recursive scan equation.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-27cb8838561eaeb340ea3669a87b464158ddccc4d0d0eeaf1e9dbd283580a136",
      "start_line": 31,
      "text": "  rule firstDivisorAtOrBelow(N:Int, D:Int)\n    => firstDivisorAtOrBelow(N, D -Int 1)\n    requires D >Int 1 andBool pyMod(N, D) =/=Int 0\n\n  // The symbolic Map backend leaves deletion of a symbolic frame as an\n  // update term.  This extensional simplification is the Map fact used by\n  // #pop: deleting the fresh key 1 restores the untouched remainder.\n  rule\n    (1 |-> _S:Scope SC:Map) [1 <- undef] => SC\n    requires notBool 1 in_keys(SC)\n    [simplification, label(deleteFreshFrame)]"
    }
  ],
